From 1abc778496e01d97cd40720cd72ec2759b6d3586 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:32:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: mark every rubble grid around the borg when the rubble
 is removed

The "You have removed the ..." handler in borg_parse_aux() is meant to
convert the rubble grids around the borg to broken doors, so a lightless
borg does not treat freshly dug ground as rubble any more. Its loops ran
a 2x2 block (y and x from c-1 to below c+1), and the loop body never
used its own x and y: it tested only the goal grid ag. With the goal
elsewhere, nothing was converted; with the goal on a rubble grid, only
that one grid converted by accident.

The correction walks the full 3x3 block around the borg and converts
each grid that is rubble. The light check keeps its meaning: the whole
handler still does nothing while the borg carries light.

Measured natively (native-c/rubblemark-192): a lightless Warrior digs a
neighbourhood of five rubble grids through the production dig command and
the game's own message reaches borg_parse; the original leaves all five
grids as rubble on the borg's map, the correction converts all five, and
the lit control is byte-identical. Investigates
diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#192.
---
 src/borg/borg-messages.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-messages.c b/src/borg/borg-messages.c
index 7adcf070e..b09f101ac 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-messages.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-messages.c
@@ -1214,9 +1214,11 @@ static void borg_parse_aux(char *msg, int len)
     /* Removed rubble.  Important when out of lite */
     if (prefix(msg, "You have removed the ")) {
         int x, y;
+        borg_grid *rx;
         /* remove rubbles from array */
-        for (y = borg.c.y - 1; y < borg.c.y + 1; y++) {
-            for (x = borg.c.x - 1; x < borg.c.x + 1; x++) {
+        for (y = borg.c.y - 1; y <= borg.c.y + 1; y++) {
+            for (x = borg.c.x - 1; x <= borg.c.x + 1; x++) {
+                rx = &borg_grids[y][x];
                 /* replace all rubble with broken doors, the borg ignores
                  * broken doors.  This routine is only needed if the borg
                  * is out of lite and searching in the dark.
@@ -1224,8 +1226,8 @@ static void borg_parse_aux(char *msg, int len)
                 if (borg.trait[BI_LIGHT])
                     continue;
 
-                if (ag->feat == FEAT_RUBBLE)
-                    ag->feat = FEAT_BROKEN;
+                if (rx->feat == FEAT_RUBBLE)
+                    rx->feat = FEAT_BROKEN;
             }
         }
         return;
